WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.710
Put a crystal of salt into
a circuit and switch on.

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.770
The bulb stays dark.

3
00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.050
Now melt that same salt.

4
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.070
Nothing is added, and
nothing is taken away.

5
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.610
Switch on again, and this
time the bulb lights.

6
00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.030
So what changed inside
the salt when it melted?

7
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.350
In this mission, you'll see what
happens when a metal meets a

8
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.000
non-metal, and electrons move
from one atom to the other.

9
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:29.170
You'll build a giant lattice of
ions and find out why it is so

10
00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:30.650
hard to melt.

11
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.670
Then you'll compare it
with small molecules,

12
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.310
where atoms share electrons.

13
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.270
Your mission: explain
why melted salt conducts,

14
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.820
but solid salt does not.
